KZ3 patch 2147 (ENHANCEMENT, experimental): an opt-in Intel XeSS Super Resolution display filter.

Off by default: Bilinear stays the default filter and with xess unselected no XeSS code runs. Selecting it
(Options > Display > Scaling filter, confirmed by a prompt, or KZ3_DISPLAY_FILTER=xess) renders the stable four-target
deferred pass with a Halton jitter applied to the scene geometry, takes its primary depth into an adapter-owned texture
at the scene copy, pairs the camera with the renderer frame being built, and upscales the last scene presentation.
The KZ3 build defines KZ3_XESS and supplies the port-owned xess.h adapter (port/kz3/xess.cpp); other ps3recomp users
compile the renderer unchanged and have no Intel SDK dependency.

Motion vectors are reconstructed from camera pose plus depth; no G-buffer is labelled as velocity, so object,
animation, vegetation, particle and shader motion are not represented. The scene resolve and the final composed frame
are paired to build XeSS's responsive-pixel mask; the display surface is captured right after the 3D compose, so
pixels the HUD then changes get zero motion and full responsiveness. Jittered frames skip FXAA (XeSS is the frame's
anti-aliasing) and get Intel's texture mip bias, log2(input / target), on the units of scene draws with a mip chain.
A dispatch checks that the camera moved on by exactly one flip: the same flip means no camera motion, a skipped flip
resets history. Re-initialising from the present path flushes the open command list first.

XeSS-SR is attempted only for a larger same-aspect output. The renderer falls back to Bilinear on an unsupported
scale, a missing or incompatible runtime, a rejected input resolution, incomplete deferred inputs or a dispatch
failure; a jittered frame that falls back holds jitter off until a dispatch works. Switching the filter away from
xess releases the context at the next present. When xess is selected the RSX_UPSCALE backend (patch 2145) is
bypassed, also on fallback; the other filters keep it.

One-run switches, read where they are used: KZ3_XESS_MIP_BIAS (default Intel's value), KZ3_XESS_CAMERA_LAG
(default 0), KZ3_XESS_HUD_MASK=0 (default on). "[xess]" lines report status, fallbacks and camera pairing.

Rules and host tests: port/kz3/xess_camera.h, xess_inputs.h, xess_motion.h with tools/smoke/test_xess_camera.c,
test_xess_inputs.c, test_xess_motion.c, test_display_mode.c, and test_xess_compile.sh (adapter compile, renderer
integration checks). tools/smoke/test_xess.cpp and test_xess_temporal.cpp need a D3D12 GPU and the Intel runtime.
Written from Intel's public XeSS SDK 3.0.2 developer guide and API headers; no game code, no Intel source.

